================================================================================
GREP CHEAT SHEET: -E (ERE) AND -P (PCRE)
================================================================================

1. ESSENTIAL FLAGS (OPTIONS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-E          Use Extended Regular Expressions (ERE).
-P          Use Perl-Compatible Regular Expressions (PCRE) - most powerful.
-i          Ignore case (A and a are the same).
-v          Invert match: select lines NOT matching the pattern.
-o          Print ONLY the matched part of the line, not the whole line.
-n          Print line number with output lines.
-l          Print ONLY names of files containing matches.
-r / -R     Recursive search in directories.
-w          Match whole words only (won't find 'cat' inside 'category').
-A [n]      Show [n] lines AFTER match.
-B [n]      Show [n] lines BEFORE match.
-C [n]      Show [n] lines around match (Context).
--color     Highlight matches (auto/always).

2. BASIC SYMBOLS (WORKS IN BOTH -E AND -P)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.           Any single character.
^           Start of a line.
$           End of a line.
*           0 or more repetitions of the previous character.
+           1 or more repetitions.
?           0 or 1 repetition.


|           Logical "OR" (e.g., "error|warning").
()          Grouping characters (capturing group).
[]          Character set (e.g., [a-z], [0-9], [AEIOU]).
[^]         Negative character set (e.g., [^0-9] - not a digit).
{n,m}       Repetition from n to m times.

3. EXCLUSIVE PCRE FEATURES (grep -P ONLY)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\d          Any digit (same as [0-9]).
\D          NOT a digit.
\w          Word character (letter, digit, or underscore).
\s          Whitespace (space, tab, newline).
\b          Word boundary.
.*?         "Lazy" match (find the shortest possible string).
(?<=...)    Lookbehind: check text on the LEFT (text is not included in match).
(?=...)     Lookahead: check text on the RIGHT (text is not included in match).

4. PRACTICAL EXAMPLES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Find IP addresses:
grep -oE '([0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}' file.txt

# Find Email addresses:
grep -oP '[\w\.-]+@[\w\.-]+\.\w+' file.txt

# Remove empty lines and comments from config:
grep -vE '^$|^#' config.conf

# Find text inside quotes (lazy match):
grep -oP '"\.*?"' file.txt

# Find 5xx HTTP errors in Nginx/Apache logs:
grep " 50[0-9] " access.log

# Extract text between [brackets] (using Lookaround):
grep -oP '(?<=\[).*?(?=\])' file.txt

# Search for "xalloc_die" in C source code recursively:
grep -Hnr '^xalloc_die' .

